1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. d4 exd4 5. O-O Be7 6. e5 Ne4 7. Nxd4 O-O 8. Nf5 d5 9. Bxc6 bxc6 10. Nxe7+ Qxe7 11. Re1 Qh4 12. Be3 f6 13. f3 fxe5 14. fxe4 d4 15. g3 { Key: 15.g3? weakens the light squares around the white king; 15.Qd2 dxe3 16.Qxe3 was better (engine +0.6 against -0.4). } 15... Qf6 16. Bxd4 exd4 17. Rf1 Qxf1+ 18. Qxf1 Rxf1+ 19. Kxf1 { Key: 17...Qxf1+ 18.Qxf1 Rxf1+ 19.Kxf1: queens and a pair of rooks are off. Black's bishop against White's knight, and a passed d-pawn for Black. } 19... Rb8 20. b3 Rb5 21. c4 Rh5 22. Kg1 c5 23. Nd2 Kf7 24. Rf1+ Ke7 25. a3 Rh6 26. h4 Ra6 27. Ra1 Bg4 28. Kf2 Ke6 29. a4 { Key: 29.a4? 29.e5 Kxe5 30.Re1+ was the active try (engine -1.8 against -2.8). In endings, a pawn move that neither makes a passed pawn nor stops one usually costs time. } 29... Ke5 30. Kg2 Rf6 31. Re1 d3 32. Rf1 Kd4 33. Rxf6 gxf6 34. Kf2 c6 35. a5 a6 36. Nb1 Kxe4 { Key: 36...Kxe4: the black king eats the centre pawn (engine -5.2). } 37. Ke1 Be2 { Key: 37...Be2? 37...Ke3 38.Nd2 Be2 was precise (engine -5.5 against -0.9). } 38. Nd2+ { Key: 38.Nd2+? misses 38.Kd2, which nearly held (engine -0.9 against -5.8). Both players missed it. } 38... Ke3 39. Nb1 f5 40. Nd2 h5 41. Nb1 Kf3 42. Nc3 Kxg3 43. Na4 f4 44. Nxc5 f3 45. Ne4+ Kf4 46. Nd6 c5 47. b4 { Key: 47.b4: desperation. The black pawns on d3 and f3 are too fast (engine -15). } 47... cxb4 48. c5 b3 49. Nc4 Kg3 0-1

