[Why "A pure knight-against-bishop ending lasting more than forty moves. Black's pawns are fixed on light squares, the colour of his own bishop, so the bishop can only defend; White's pawns stand on dark squares where the bishop cannot touch them. The engine finds several positions where White would win more easily if Black had to move, and Schlechter's knight tours the board to hand him the move: zugzwang decided by tempo moves."]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 f5 4. Bf4 c6 5. e3 Nf6 6. Bd3 Be7 7. Nf3 O-O 8. O-O Ne4 9. Bxe4 fxe4 { Key: 9.Bxe4 fxe4: the pawn on e4 cramps White, but the f-pawn can undermine it, and 15.f4 does. } 10. Ne5 Nd7 11. Qe2 Nxe5 12. Bxe5 Bd6 13. Bxd6 Qxd6 14. c5 Qe7 15. f4 exf3 16. Rxf3 Rxf3 17. Qxf3 e5 18. Rf1 exd4 19. exd4 Bd7 20. h3 Re8 21. Rf2 Rf8 22. Qxf8+ Qxf8 23. Rxf8+ Kxf8 { Key: 22.Qxf8+ Qxf8 23.Rxf8+ Kxf8: knight against bishop. Black's pawns on c6 and d5 stand on light squares, the colour of his own bishop; White's pawns on c5 and d4 stand on dark squares, out of its reach. } 24. Nd1 Ke7 25. Ne3 Kf6 26. h4 Bf5 27. b4 Bd3 28. Kf2 h5 29. Kf3 g5 30. g3 Be4+ 31. Ke2 Kg6 32. Kd2 Kf6 33. Kc3 Bg6 34. b5 Be4 35. a4 gxh4 36. gxh4 Ke6 37. Kb4 Bd3 38. b6 a6 39. a5 Be4 40. Kc3 Kf6 41. Kd2 Bf5 42. Ke1 Be4 43. Kf2 Ke6 44. Kg3 Kf7 45. Kf4 Kf6 { Key: Here the engine rates the position +1.2 with White to move but +4.0 if Black had to move: White needs to lose a tempo. From the next move the knight tours the board (f1, g3, h1, f2, d1, c3, a2, b4, d3, e5) to do it. } 46. Nf1 Bf5 47. Ng3 Bg4 48. Nh1 Be6 49. Nf2 Bf5 50. Nd1 Bg4 51. Nc3 Bd7 52. Na2 Be6 53. Nb4 Bc8 54. Nd3 Bf5 55. Ne5 Bc8 56. Ke3 Ke6 { Key: Again the engine prefers Black to move (+3.0 against +0.9): the knight's tempo moves keep the black king and bishop at the limit. } 57. Ng6 Kf6 58. Kf4 Bd7 59. Ne5 Bc8 60. Nf3 { Key: 60.Nf3? 60.Kf3 kept the bind (engine +3.7 against +1.3). } 60... Bf5 { Key: 60...Bf5? returns the chance; 60...Bg4 was the defence (engine +1.3 against +3.3). } 61. Ke3 Bc8 62. Ne5 Ke6 63. Kf3 Ke7 64. Nd3 Bf5 65. Nf4 Bg4+ 66. Ke3 Kf7 67. Nd3 Ke7 68. Ne5 Bc8 69. Kf3 Ke6 70. Nd3 Kf6 71. Ke3 1-0

