1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 e5 4. e3 exd4 5. exd4 Nf6 6. Nf3 Be7 7. Bd3 O-O 8. h3 dxc4 9. Bxc4 { Key: 8...dxc4 9.Bxc4: White has an isolated queen's pawn on d4. In return his pieces develop freely and the e-file is his. } 9... Nbd7 10. O-O Nb6 11. Bd3 Nbd5 { Key: 11...Nbd5: Black puts a knight on d5, the blockade square in front of the isolated pawn. } 12. Re1 Re8 13. Bg5 Be6 14. Qd2 h6 15. Bh4 Nh5 16. Bxe7 Rxe7 17. Re5 { Key: 17.Re5: the rook uses e5, a square the d4 pawn guards, to join the attack. } 17... Nhf6 18. Rae1 Qd6 19. Bc4 Rae8 20. Bb3 Nb6 21. Qe2 Kf8 22. Ne4 Nxe4 23. Qxe4 Bxb3 24. axb3 Nd7 25. Qh7 { Key: 25.Qh7: the queen reaches the king's door; the black king has already run to f8. } 25... Nf6 26. Qf5 Qd7 27. Qf4 Nd5 28. Rxe7 Rxe7 29. Rxe7 Kxe7 30. Qe5+ Kf8 31. Qb8+ Ke7 32. Ne5 Qc7 33. Qg8 Kf6 34. Qh7 Qb6 { Key: 34...Qb6?? walks into a fork; 34...Qe7 was the defence (engine +1.3 against +6.6). } 35. Nd7+ { Key: 35.Nd7+ forks the king on f6 and the queen on b6. } 1-0

