1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 exd4 4. Qxd4 Nc6 5. Bb5 Bd7 6. Bxc6 Bxc6 7. Bg5 f6 8. Bh4 Nh6 9. Nc3 Qd7 10. O-O Be7 11. Rad1 O-O 12. Qc4+ Rf7 13. Nd4 Ng4 14. h3 Ne5 15. Qe2 g5 16. Bg3 Rg7 17. Nf5 { Key: 17.Nf5: a knight on f5, defended by the e4 pawn. Black's g-pawn has gone to g5 and his e-pawn is gone, so no pawn can ever chase it. } 17... Rg6 18. f4 gxf4 19. Rxf4 { Key: 18.f4 gxf4 19.Rxf4: the f-file opens towards the black king. } 19... Kh8 20. Rh4 Bf8 21. Bxe5 fxe5 22. Rf1 Qe6 23. Nb5 Qg8 24. Rf2 a6 { Key: 24...a6? 24...Rd8 kept Black closer (engine +1.3 against +2.3). } 25. Nxc7 { Key: 25.Nxc7 wins a pawn. } 25... Rc8 26. Nd5 Bxd5 27. exd5 Rc7 28. c4 Be7 29. Rh5 Qe8 { Key: 29...Qe8? 29...Bf8 was more solid (engine +2.4 against +3.8). } 30. c5 Rxc5 { Key: 30...Rxc5?? takes a pawn and allows the finish; 30...Qb8 was necessary (engine +3.9 against +6.0). } 31. Rxh7+ { Key: 31.Rxh7+ Kxh7 32.Qh5+ Kg8 33.Nxe7+: the rook sacrifice brings the queen to h5 with check, and the knight joins. } 31... Kxh7 32. Qh5+ Kg8 33. Nxe7+ Kg7 34. Nf5+ Kg8 35. Nxd6 1-0

