1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 c5 3. c4 e6 4. e3 Nf6 5. Bd3 Nc6 6. O-O Bd6 7. b3 O-O 8. Bb2 b6 9. Nbd2 Bb7 10. Rc1 Qe7 11. cxd5 exd5 12. Nh4 g6 13. Nhf3 Rad8 14. dxc5 bxc5 { Key: 14.dxc5 bxc5: Black has hanging pawns on c5 and d5, side by side with no pawn next to them. They are strong while they control the centre and weak if they can be blockaded. } 15. Bb5 Ne4 16. Bxc6 Bxc6 17. Qc2 Nxd2 18. Nxd2 d4 { Key: 18...d4! The pawn advances to open the long diagonal for the bishop on c6; the bishop on d6 already aims at h2 (engine -0.7). } 19. exd4 { Key: 19.exd4? opens the lines; 19.g3 was the defence (engine -0.7 against -3.2). } 19... Bxh2+ { Key: 19...Bxh2+ 20.Kxh2 Qh4+ 21.Kg1 Bxg2: both bishops are given to strip the white king. } 20. Kxh2 Qh4+ 21. Kg1 Bxg2 22. f3 Rfe8 23. Ne4 Qh1+ 24. Kf2 Bxf1 25. d5 f5 26. Qc3 { Key: 26.Qc3 allows a forced mate (engine: mate in 5). } 26... Qg2+ 27. Ke3 Rxe4+ 28. fxe4 f4+ { Key: 28...f4+ wins too, but 28...Qg3+ 29.Kd2 Qf2+ 30.Kd1 Qe2# was faster (mate in 3). } 29. Kxf4 Rf8+ 30. Ke5 Qh2+ 31. Ke6 Re8+ 32. Kd7 Bb5# 0-1

