1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. b4 { Key: 3.b4: White's bishop goes to b2 and the long diagonal. } 3... Bg7 4. Bb2 O-O 5. g3 b6 6. Bg2 Bb7 7. O-O d6 8. d3 Nbd7 9. Nbd2 e5 10. Qc2 Re8 11. Rfd1 a5 12. a3 h6 13. Nf1 c5 14. b5 Nf8 15. e3 Qc7 16. d4 Be4 17. Qc3 exd4 18. exd4 N6d7 { Key: 18...N6d7? 18...Ne6 19.dxc5 kept Black level (engine -0.7 against +0.4). } 19. Qd2 cxd4 20. Bxd4 Qxc4 { Key: 20...Qxc4 takes a pawn but loses time; 20...Nf6 21.Qb2 was safer (engine +0.4 against +1.2). } 21. Bxg7 Kxg7 22. Qb2+ { Key: 21.Bxg7 Kxg7 22.Qb2+: White trades the fianchetto bishop and checks on the long diagonal. } 22... Kg8 23. Rxd6 { Key: 23.Rxd6: the pawn comes back and the rook is active on the sixth rank. } 23... Qc5 24. Rad1 Ra7 25. Ne3 Qh5 26. Nd4 Bxg2 27. Kxg2 Qe5 28. Nc4 Qc5 29. Nc6 Rc7 30. Ne3 Ne5 { Key: 30...Ne5? 30...Rxe3 31.fxe3 Qxe3 was the try (engine +1.8 against +3.5). } 31. R1d5 { Key: 31.R1d5 attacks the queen on c5, and Capablanca resigned. } 1-0

