1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Ba5 6. O-O d6 7. d4 exd4 8. cxd4 Nf6 9. e5 dxe5 10. Ba3 Be6 11. Bb5 Qd5 12. Qa4 O-O-O { Key: 12...O-O-O is risky with the b-file open; 12...Bd7 was the engine's choice (-0.4 against +0.4). } 13. Bxc6 bxc6 14. Bc5 Bb6 15. Qa6+ { Key: 15.Qa6+? 15.Nxe5 kept the initiative (engine +0.5 against -1.3). } 15... Kb8 16. Nxe5 Nd7 17. Nc3 { Key: 17.Nc3? 17.Nxd7+ was necessary (engine -0.6 against -2.3). } 17... Nxc5 18. Qe2 Qd6 19. dxc5 Qxc5 20. Na4 Qb5 21. Qxb5 cxb5 22. Nxb6 axb6 23. Nc6+ Kb7 24. Nxd8+ Rxd8 { Key: 23.Nc6+ Kb7 24.Nxd8+ Rxd8: White wins the exchange, but Black has two extra pawns and the engine prefers Black (-1.9). } 25. a3 c5 26. f3 Kc6 27. Rfd1 Ra8 28. Kf2 Ra4 29. Ke3 h5 30. Kd2 b4 31. axb4 Rxb4 32. Rdb1 Rxb1 33. Rxb1 b5 34. Ra1 b4 35. Kc2 Kd5 36. Rd1+ Kc4 37. Rd8 Bd5 38. h4 Kd4 39. Rb8 Be6 40. Rb7 g6 41. Rb5 b3+ 42. Kb2 c4 { Key: 41...b3+ 42.Kb2 c4: two connected passed pawns, supported by king and bishop, beat the rook (engine -5.8). } 43. Rb4 Kd3 44. Rb6 c3+ 45. Kb1 Ke3 0-1

