1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d5 { Key: 2...d5? The Elephant Gambit gives a pawn without enough development in return; 2...Nc6 was normal (engine +0.8). } 3. exd5 e4 4. Qe2 Qe7 5. Nd4 Qe5 6. Nb5 { Key: 4.Qe2 Qe7 5.Nd4 Qe5 6.Nb5: both sides have moved one piece three times, but 6.Nb5 threatens Nxc7+. } 6... Bd6 { Key: 6...Bd6? 6...Bb4 was better (engine +1.6 against +2.3). } 7. d4 Qe7 8. c4 Bb4+ 9. Bd2 Bxd2+ 10. Nxd2 a6 { Key: 10...a6? Another pawn move; 10...Nf6 developed. After ten moves Black has not developed a single knight (engine +2.5). } 11. Nc3 f5 12. O-O-O { Key: 12.O-O-O: White castles and his rook lands on the d-file at once. } 12... Nf6 13. Re1 O-O 14. f3 b5 15. fxe4 fxe4 16. Ndxe4 bxc4 17. Qxc4 Kh8 18. Bd3 Bb7 { Key: 18...Bb7? 18...Bf5 was more stubborn (engine +3.3 against +5.1). } 19. Nxf6 Qxf6 20. Rhf1 Qd8 { Key: 20...Qd8? 20...Qg5+ was the try (engine +4.3 against +5.5). } 21. Rxf8+ Qxf8 22. Qb4 1-0

